From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:59:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AudioSourceInstance::seek: refuse scratch smaller than one
 frame

The generic decode-and-discard loop computed mScratchSize / mChannels
frames per pass; with less than one frame of scratch (or zero channels)
that was 0 and the loop never terminated. A negative target after rewind
also made the counter negative. Reject undersized scratch up front and
loop only while frames remain.

Fixes upstream #392.
---
 src/core/soloud_audiosource.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud_audiosource.cpp b/src/core/soloud_audiosource.cpp
index 3123f8f..ea11a01 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud_audiosource.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud_audiosource.cpp
@@ -156,6 +156,10 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	result AudioSourceInstance::seek(double aSeconds, float *mScratch, unsigned int mScratchSize)
 	{
+		// The discard loop below needs room for at least one frame per pass.
+		if (mChannels == 0 || mScratch == NULL || mScratchSize < mChannels)
+			return INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
 		double offset = aSeconds - mStreamPosition;
 		if (offset <= 0)
 		{
@@ -168,7 +172,7 @@ namespace SoLoud
 		}
 		int samples_to_discard = (int)floor(mSamplerate * offset);
 
-		while (samples_to_discard)
+		while (samples_to_discard > 0)
 		{
 			int samples = mScratchSize / mChannels;
 			if (samples > samples_to_discard)
